<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::escalation_pressure" target="ai_governance_cyber_risk::regulatory_pressure" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising political and operational pressure to escalate (including weaponization or offensive AI use) produces high-profile incidents and strategic concern that prompt legislators and regulators to accelerate rulemaking, export controls and oversight of AI capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_governance_cyber_risk</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::escalation_pressure" target="global_energy_volatility::global_oil_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Elevated political and military pressure that raises the risk of wider strikes on energy infrastructure or broader supply disruption prompts markets to price in a higher supply-risk premium, pushing up crude prices.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_volatility</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::escalation_pressure" target="iran_hormuz_standoff::security_incident_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Heightened escalation pressure in the Russia–Ukraine war prompts redeployment of Western naval and intelligence assets toward the European theatre, reducing patrols and deterrent presence in the Persian Gulf and thereby enabling increased Iranian harassment, seizures, or strikes on commercial shipping.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_hormuz_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::escalation_pressure" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::trade_control_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising political and operational pressure to prevent further escalation prompts governments to broaden and tighten export controls and licensing on dual‑use and high‑end technologies, raising overall trade control levels.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::escalation_pressure" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::cross_border_capital" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher escalation increases investor risk aversion and triggers sanctions/screening of outbound/inbound strategic investment, directly reducing cross‑border capital flows into sensitive tech sectors.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
