<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::trade_control_level" target="ai_governance_cyber_risk::ai_investment_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter export controls and licensing uncertainty cause investors (both domestic risk-averse VCs and foreign limited partners) to withhold or reroute funding from firms whose addressable markets or supply access are curtailed, reducing capital deployment into AI projects.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_governance_cyber_risk</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::trade_control_level" target="ai_governance_cyber_risk::model_productization" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Restrictions on export of accelerators, development toolchains and pretrained assets directly prevent companies from acquiring necessary hardware and software components, delaying or blocking the conversion of research models into deployable commercial products.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_governance_cyber_risk</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::trade_control_level" target="global_energy_volatility::tanker_risk_premium" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Stricter US-China export controls and licensing enforcement provoke interdictions, sanctions‑related boardings and increased naval/escort deployments along key shipping routes, raising insurers' and charterers' perceived war/contingency risk and thus the tanker risk premium.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_volatility</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::trade_control_level" target="russia_ukraine_war::drone_attack_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter export controls on advanced semiconductors and avionics destined for China reduce the pool of re‑exportable/high‑end chips that find their way to Russian drone manufacturers, degrading guidance/EW capability and lowering the rate of effective drone attacks within months.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
