  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Improved supply‑chain resilience (better insurance, naval escorts, diversified logistics guarantees) reduces firms' risk premiums for using the shortest sea routes, prompting shippers and energy traders to route more cargo through the Strait and thus raising maritime throughput.</data>
