<edge source="global_energy_volatility::tanker_risk_premium" target="ai_governance_cyber_risk::model_productization" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising tanker risk premiums increase shipping delays and insurance costs for imported GPUs, servers and other compute hardware, lengthening supply chains and slowing the timeline for converting models into customer-facing products.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_energy_volatility</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_governance_cyber_risk</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_volatility::tanker_risk_premium" target="iran_hormuz_standoff::maritime_throughput_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher insurance and security surcharges for tankers transiting the corridor make passage through Hormuz less economically viable, prompting shippers to reduce transits or reroute and thereby lowering throughput.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_energy_volatility</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_hormuz_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_volatility::tanker_risk_premium" target="russia_ukraine_war::trade_flow_disruption" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">An increased tanker risk premium raises voyage costs and insurer refusal rates for vessels transiting the Black Sea and nearby routes, prompting route avoidance, cancellations and port service gaps that quickly translate into measurable interruptions of trade flows tied to the Russia–Ukraine corridor.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_energy_volatility</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
